       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Requested:** metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Single doses are typically no more than 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** The requested total is about twice the maximum. It raises the risk of serious lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Possible intended doses include 850 mg TID (2,550 mg/day), 1,000 mg BID (2,000 mg/day), or 500 mg TID.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 1,700 mg TID, for example because of an unusual clinical situation, tell me. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
